Check HasProperty before Get when a global reference reaches a proxy.

A global identifier is resolved with HasBinding on the global object's
environment record, which calls HasProperty, and only then Get.
JS_GetPropertyInternal called a proxy's get trap at once when the
proxy sat in the global object's prototype chain, so an unknown name
evaluated to undefined instead of throwing ReferenceError. Aura puts
the window's named properties object (window.foo for an element with
id foo) there as a proxy, as the HTML Standard places it. With
throw_ref_error set the has trap now runs first, and a false answer
throws ReferenceError. Property reads (throw_ref_error unset) are
unchanged.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -9350,10 +9350,22 @@
                 if (em) {
                     if (em->get_property) {
                         JSValue obj1, retval;
-                        /* XXX: should pass throw_ref_error */
                         /* Note: if 'p' is a prototype, it can be
                            freed in the called function */
                         obj1 = js_dup(JS_MKPTR(JS_TAG_OBJECT, p));
+                        if (unlikely(throw_ref_error) && em->has_property) {
+                            /* A global reference: HasBinding first
+                               (HasProperty), so a proxy in the global
+                               object's prototype chain that does not
+                               have the name leaves it unresolvable. */
+                            int has = em->has_property(ctx, obj1, prop);
+                            if (has <= 0) {
+                                JS_FreeValue(ctx, obj1);
+                                if (has < 0)
+                                    return JS_EXCEPTION;
+                                return JS_ThrowReferenceErrorNotDefined(ctx, prop);
+                            }
+                        }
                         retval = em->get_property(ctx, obj1, prop, this_obj);
                         JS_FreeValue(ctx, obj1);
                         return retval;
